{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"comm -3 <(nm -D --defined-only c_src/build/libdag_c.so | awk '\"'$2 ~ /''^[TDBR]$/ {print $3}'\"' | sort) <(sed -n 's/\"'^| [0-9][0-9]* | `'\"\\\\([\"'^`]*'\"\\\\)\"'`.*/'\"\\\\1/p' SYMBOLS.md | sort); sed -n '1,220p' ERRORS.md; sed -n '1,260p' CONFIGS.md\"","aggregated_output":"shallow_copy\n# Error Surface\n\nRows are derived from every error return, null check, capacity/range check,\nallocation check, and not-found sentinel in `c_src/src/lib.c`. Internal\nrecursive guards are exercised through `shallow_copy`.\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n| 1 | `create_graph` | `malloc(sizeof(graph_t)) == NULL` | Return `NULL`. |\n| 2 | `add_node` | `graph == NULL` or `city_name == NULL` | Return `NULL`. |\n| 3 | `add_node` | `graph->node_count >= MAX_NODES` (100) | Return `NULL`. |\n| 4 | `add_node` | An existing stored `city_name` is exactly equal to the input under `strcmp` | Return `NULL`. |\n| 5 | `add_node` | `malloc(sizeof(node_t)) == NULL` | Return `NULL` without incrementing `node_count`. |\n| 6 | `add_edge` | `from == NULL` or `to == NULL` | Return `-1`. |\n| 7 | `add_edge` | `from->edge_count >= MAX_EDGES` (10) | Return `-1`. |\n| 8 | `add_edge` | `distance < 0` | Return `-1`. |\n| 9 | `add_edge` | An existing edge has `destination == to` | Return `-1`. |\n| 10 | `delete_node` | `node == NULL` | Return normally without action. |\n| 11 | `delete_node` | Decrement makes `node->ref_count == 0` | Free the node and return normally. |\n| 12 | `increment_refs_recursive` via `shallow_copy` | Recursive `node == NULL` | Return from that recursive branch without action. |\n| 13 | `increment_refs_recursive` via `shallow_copy` | Node pointer is already in `visited` | Return from that recursive branch without a second increment. |\n| 14 | `increment_refs_recursive` via `shallow_copy` | `*visited_count >= MAX_NODES` | Do not append to `visited`; continue incrementing and traversing. |\n| 15 | `shallow_copy` | `start == NULL` | Return `NULL`. |\n| 16 | `find_shortest_path` | `start == NULL`, `end == NULL`, or `path_length == NULL` | Return `NULL`; do not write a length. |\n| 17 | `find_shortest_path` | End node is absent from state or retains distance `INT_MAX` | Set `*path_length = 0` and return `NULL`. |\n| 18 | `find_shortest_path` | `malloc(sizeof(node_t*) * count) == NULL` | Set `*path_length = 0` and return `NULL`. |\n| 19 | `get_node_by_name` | `graph == NULL` or `city_name == NULL` | Return `NULL`. |\n| 20 | `get_node_by_name` | No stored name compares equal to `city_name` | Return `NULL`. |\n| 21 | `print_node` | `node == NULL` | Write `NULL node\\n` to stdout and return. |\n| 22 | `print_graph` | `graph == NULL` | Write `NULL graph\\n` to stdout and return. |\n| 23 | `free_graph` | `graph == NULL` | Return normally without action. |\n# Configuration Surface\n\n## Build-Time Configurations\n\n`Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` table and `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` has no CMake\noptions or conditional definitions. There is exactly one valid combination:\n\n| # | Rust features | C configuration | [ ] |\n|---|---------------|-----------------|-----|\n| B1 | No features (`--no-default-features`) | Default CMake configuration with position-independent code | [ ] |\n\n## Runtime and Input Configurations\n\nThe public header exposes no runtime option flags or enums. Rows below are the\ncross-product pruned to distinctions present in C branches, loops, constants,\nand pointer-identity comparisons. `MAX_CITY_NAME = 64`, `MAX_EDGES = 10`, and\n`MAX_NODES = 100`.\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1 | `create_graph` | Empty graph initialization: count 0 and all 100 node slots null | [ ] |\n| 2 | `add_node` | First node; empty city name (length 0) | [ ] |\n| 3 | `add_node` | First node; short city name (length 1..62) | [ ] |\n| 4 | `add_node` | First node; boundary city name (length 63) | [ ] |\n| 5 | `add_node` | First node; long city name (length >=64), truncated to 63 bytes and terminated | [ ] |\n| 6 | `add_node` | Nonempty graph below capacity; unique name exercises existing-node scan | [ ] |\n| 7 | `add_node`, `get_node_by_name` | Long-name asymmetry: stored truncated name is found by its 63-byte form, while the original long form is not equal | [ ] |\n| 8 | `add_node` | Boundary valid insertion at prior `node_count == 99`, producing 100 nodes | [ ] |\n| 9 | `get_node_by_name` | Match first node in a one-node graph | [ ] |\n| 10 | `get_node_by_name` | Match a later node after one or more failed comparisons | [ ] |\n| 11 | `add_edge` | Distinct nodes, first outgoing edge, zero distance | [ ] |\n| 12 | `add_edge` | Distinct nodes, first outgoing edge, positive distance | [ ] |\n| 13 | `add_edge` | Self-edge (`from == to`) | [ ] |\n| 14 | `add_edge` | Boundary valid insertion at prior `edge_count == 9`, producing 10 edges | [ ] |\n| 15 | `delete_node` | Reference count greater than 1: decrement without freeing | [ ] |\n| 16 | `shallow_copy` | Isolated start node: increment only the start | [ ] |\n| 17 | `shallow_copy` | Linear reachable chain with one or many edges | [ ] |\n| 18 | `shallow_copy` | Branches that merge on one destination: increment each pointer once | [ ] |\n| 19 | `shallow_copy` | Directed cycle/self-edge: visited-pointer guard terminates recursion and increments each node once | [ ] |\n| 20 | `find_shortest_path` | `start == end`: one-node path | [ ] |\n| 21 | `find_shortest_path` | Direct edge: two-node path | [ ] |\n| 22 | `find_shortest_path` | Linear chain: multi-node path reconstruction and reversal | [ ] |\n| 23 | `find_shortest_path` | Competing routes with different total distances: choose lower total | [ ] |\n| 24 | `find_shortest_path` | Equal-distance alternatives: retain first predecessor because update uses strict `<` | [ ] |\n| 25 | `find_shortest_path` | Zero-distance edges mixed with positive edges | [ ] |\n| 26 | `find_shortest_path` | Reachable graph containing a directed cycle | [ ] |\n| 27 | `find_shortest_path` | Boundary reachable state of 100 nodes | [ ] |\n| 28 | `print_node` | Node with zero outgoing edges | [ ] |\n| 29 | `print_node` | Node with one or many outgoing edges | [ ] |\n| 30 | `print_graph` | Empty graph | [ ] |\n| 31 | `print_graph` | Graph with one or many nodes and their edges | [ ] |\n| 32 | `free_graph` | Empty graph | [ ] |\n| 33 | `free_graph`, `delete_node` | Graph node at ref count 1: graph cleanup decrements to zero and frees it | [ ] |\n| 34 | `free_graph`, `shallow_copy` | Graph nodes with ref count greater than 1: graph cleanup decrements but does not free them | [ ] |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
